{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectHotkey"},{"type":"text","value":" API is the primary way to register keyboard shortcuts in Angular applications. It wraps the singleton "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeyManager"},{"type":"text","value":" with injection-context lifecycle management and Angular signal-friendly reactive options."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"logical-keys-and-physical-positions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Logical keys and physical positions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use a logical binding when the shortcut should follow the character on the active layout. Use a physical binding when it should follow a keyboard position:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Binding"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Identity checked"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Mod+S"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ key: 'S', mod: true }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Logical "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"event.key"},{"type":"text","value":", with conservative code fallback"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Mod+[KeyS]"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ code: 'KeyS', mod: true }"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exact "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"event.code"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Enter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Logical Enter, including numpad Enter"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[Enter]"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[NumpadEnter]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Separate physical Enter positions"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every physical code uses brackets in strings, including names shared with logical keys such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[Enter]"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[F13]"},{"type":"text","value":". Supported codes are type-safe and available in autocomplete. Do not put a bracketed code in an object's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"},{"type":"text","value":" field; use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code"},{"type":"text","value":". A binding has either "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"key"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"code"},{"type":"text","value":", never both."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On a layout where the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"KeyQ"},{"type":"text","value":" position produces "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"a"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"A"},{"type":"text","value":" follows that character and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[KeyQ]"},{"type":"text","value":" follows the position. Logical ASCII letters remain layout-aware; conservative physical fallback helps with transformed output such as macOS Option keys. Exact matches take priority over weaker fallbacks among eligible registrations on the same target."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Callbacks expose the same distinction in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context.parsedHotkey"},{"type":"text","value":": check "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parsed.code !== undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" before reading its physical identity. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"formatForDisplay"},{"type":"text","value":" for labels; stored physical strings retain their brackets."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic usage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectHotkey } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\n@Component({ standalone: true, template: `` })\nexport class AppComponent {\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkey('Mod+S', () => {\n      saveDocument()\n    })\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The callback receives the original "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"KeyboardEvent"},{"type":"text","value":" as the first argument and a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeyCallbackContext"},{"type":"text","value":" as the second:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"injectHotkey('Mod+S', (event, context) => {\n  console.log(context.hotkey)\n  console.log(context.parsedHotkey)\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"changing-a-binding","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changing a binding"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass a new logical or physical binding through your framework's normal state mechanism. A recorder result such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Alt+[KeyS]"},{"type":"text","value":" can be passed directly to the same registration API. Keep an initial binding in application state if you want a reset button; the library does not need a separate preferences store."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"property-getters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Property getters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Property getters and functions returning an options object are both supported. Read reactive state inside the getter. A plain value such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ enabled: currentValue }"},{"type":"text","value":" captures the value when that object is created."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter reads option properties inside its reactive computation and updates registrations automatically. Callbacks such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onRecord"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCancel"},{"type":"text","value":" remain functions; the adapter does not call them to resolve options. Tracking is shallow; callback bodies and nested objects are not evaluated to discover dependencies. Keep getters free of side effects. Ordinary option changes preserve registration identity. Changing the target moves the registration to that target."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Component, signal } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectHotkey } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\n@Component({ selector: 'save-shortcut', template: '' })\nexport class SaveShortcut {\n\tenabled = signal(true)\n\n\tconstructor() {\n\t\tconst component = this\n\t\tinjectHotkey('Mod+S', () => console.log('Save'), {\n\t\t\tget enabled() {\n\t\t\t\treturn component.enabled()\n\t\t\t},\n\t\t})\n\t}\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can also pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"() => ({ enabled: this.enabled() })"},{"type":"text","value":" from the component. Signals read by option getters update registrations when Angular runs the effect. Use the same forms for common options, per-definition options, sequences, and recorders. Getter properties in provided defaults are tracked too."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"default-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectHotkey"},{"type":"text","value":" uses the same core defaults as the framework-agnostic manager:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"injectHotkey('Mod+S', callback, {\n  enabled: true,\n  preventDefault: true,\n  stopPropagation: true,\n  eventType: 'keydown',\n  requireReset: false,\n  ignoreInputs: undefined,\n  target: document,\n  platform: undefined,\n  conflictBehavior: 'warn',\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"reactive-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reactive options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For reactive state, pass an options object with property getters or a function returning options."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"enabled","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enabled"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enabled"},{"type":"text","value":" is false, the hotkey stays registered (visible in devtools); only the callback is suppressed."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Component, signal } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectHotkey } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\n@Component({ standalone: true, template: `` })\nexport class EditorComponent {\n  readonly isEditing = signal(false)\n\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkey('Mod+S', () => save(), () => ({\n      enabled: this.isEditing(),\n    }))\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"target","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"target"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Component, ElementRef, viewChild } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectHotkey } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\n@Component({\n  standalone: true,\n  template: `<div #panel tabindex=\"0\">Panel content</div>`,\n})\nexport class PanelComponent {\n  private readonly panel = viewChild<ElementRef<HTMLDivElement>>('panel')\n\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkey('Escape', () => closePanel(), () => ({\n      target: this.panel()?.nativeElement ?? null,\n    }))\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"global-defaults-via-provider","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Global defaults via provider"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { ApplicationConfig } from '@angular/core'\nimport { provideHotkeys } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\nexport const appConfig: ApplicationConfig = {\n  providers: [\n    provideHotkeys({\n      hotkey: { preventDefault: false, ignoreInputs: false },\n    }),\n  ],\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common options"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"requirereset","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requireReset"}]},{"type":"code","value":"injectHotkey('Escape', () => closePanel(), { requireReset: true })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"ignoreinputs","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ignoreInputs"}]},{"type":"code","value":"injectHotkey('K', () => openSearch())\ninjectHotkey('Enter', () => submit(), { ignoreInputs: false })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"conflictbehavior","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"conflictBehavior"}]},{"type":"code","value":"injectHotkey('Mod+S', () => save(), { conflictBehavior: 'replace' })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"platform","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"platform"}]},{"type":"code","value":"injectHotkey('Mod+S', () => save(), { platform: 'mac' })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"automatic-cleanup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Automatic cleanup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Registrations are cleaned up automatically when the owning injection context is destroyed."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"registering-multiple-hotkeys","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Registering multiple hotkeys"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When you need to register several hotkeys at once, or a dynamic list of variable length, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectHotkeys"},{"type":"text","value":" (plural):"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectHotkeys } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\n@Component({ standalone: true, template: `` })\nexport class EditorComponent {\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkeys([\n      { hotkey: 'Mod+S', callback: () => this.save() },\n      { hotkey: 'Mod+Z', callback: () => this.undo() },\n      { hotkey: 'Escape', callback: () => this.close() },\n    ])\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"common-options-with-per-hotkey-overrides","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common options with per-hotkey overrides"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass shared options as the second argument. Per-definition options override the common ones:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"injectHotkeys(\n  [\n    { hotkey: 'Mod+S', callback: () => this.save() },\n    { hotkey: 'Mod+Z', callback: () => this.undo(), options: { enabled: false } },\n  ],\n  { preventDefault: true },\n)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"dynamic-hotkey-lists","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dynamic hotkey lists"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass a getter for reactive arrays driven by Angular signals:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"shortcuts = signal([...])\n\nconstructor() {\n  injectHotkeys(\n    () => this.shortcuts().map((s) => ({\n      hotkey: s.key,\n      callback: s.action,\n    })),\n  )\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The function tracks signal dependencies and diffs registrations automatically."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"metadata-name-description-and-group","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Metadata (name, description, and group)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every hotkey registration can carry a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"meta"},{"type":"text","value":" object with a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"description"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group"},{"type":"text","value":". Metadata never affects hotkey behavior, but it flows through to registrations and devtools, so you can build shortcut palettes and help screens from it."}]},{"type":"code","value":"injectHotkey('Mod+S', () => save(), {\n  meta: { name: 'Save', description: 'Save the document' },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"meta"},{"type":"text","value":" option is typed as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeyMeta"},{"type":"text","value":", which ships with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"description"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"group"},{"type":"text","value":" fields. You can extend it with additional properties using TypeScript declaration merging:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"declare module '@tanstack/hotkeys' {\n  interface HotkeyMeta {\n    icon?: string\n  }\n}\n\ninjectHotkey('Mod+S', () => save(), {\n  meta: { name: 'Save', description: 'Save the document', icon: 'floppy', group: 'File' },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Group is descriptive metadata, not an execution scope. A shortcuts panel can group live registration views directly. Disabled registrations remain listed; unmounted registrations disappear."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"introspecting-registrations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Introspecting registrations"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectHotkeyRegistrations"},{"type":"text","value":" API to get a live view of all hotkey and sequence registrations. Use it to build shortcut palettes, help dialogs, or devtools."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectHotkeyRegistrations, formatForDisplay } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\n@Component({\n  standalone: true,\n  template: `\n    <h2>Keyboard Shortcuts</h2>\n    <ul>\n      @for (reg of registrations().hotkeys; track reg.id) {\n        <li>\n          <kbd>{{ formatForDisplay(reg.hotkey) }}</kbd>\n          @if (reg.options.meta?.name) {\n            <span> — {{ reg.options.meta.name }}</span>\n          }\n          @if (reg.options.meta?.description) {\n            <p>{{ reg.options.meta.description }}</p>\n          }\n        </li>\n      }\n    </ul>\n    @if (registrations().sequences.length > 0) {\n      <h2>Sequences</h2>\n      <ul>\n        @for (reg of registrations().sequences; track reg.id) {\n          <li>\n            <kbd>{{ displaySequence(reg.sequence) }}</kbd>\n            @if (reg.options.meta?.name) {\n              <span> — {{ reg.options.meta.name }}</span>\n            }\n          </li>\n        }\n      </ul>\n    }\n  `,\n})\nexport class ShortcutPaletteComponent {\n  readonly formatForDisplay = formatForDisplay\n  readonly displaySequence = (sequence: ReadonlyArray<Parameters<typeof formatForDisplay>[0]>) =>\n    sequence.map((step) => formatForDisplay(step)).join(' → ')\n  readonly registrations = injectHotkeyRegistrations()\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The returned signal holds an object with two arrays. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hotkeys"},{"type":"text","value":" contains registration objects with the hotkey string, options (including "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"meta"},{"type":"text","value":"), and enabled state. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sequences"},{"type":"text","value":" contains sequence registrations with the same structure."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-hotkey-manager","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hotkey manager"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can access the underlying manager directly when needed:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { getHotkeyManager } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\nconst manager = getHotkeyManager()\nmanager.isRegistered('Mod+S')\nmanager.getRegistrationCount()","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"logical-keys-and-physical-positions","text":"Logical keys and physical positions","level":2},{"id":"basic-usage","text":"Basic usage","level":2},{"id":"changing-a-binding","text":"Changing a binding","level":3},{"id":"property-getters","text":"Property getters","level":2},{"id":"default-options","text":"Default options","level":2},{"id":"reactive-options","text":"Reactive options","level":2},{"id":"enabled","text":"enabled","level":3},{"id":"target","text":"target","level":3},{"id":"global-defaults-via-provider","text":"Global defaults via provider","level":2},{"id":"common-options","text":"Common options","level":2},{"id":"requirereset","text":"requireReset","level":3},{"id":"ignoreinputs","text":"ignoreInputs","level":3},{"id":"conflictbehavior","text":"conflictBehavior","level":3},{"id":"platform","text":"platform","level":3},{"id":"automatic-cleanup","text":"Automatic cleanup","level":2},{"id":"registering-multiple-hotkeys","text":"Registering multiple hotkeys","level":2},{"id":"common-options-with-per-hotkey-overrides","text":"Common options with per-hotkey overrides","level":3},{"id":"dynamic-hotkey-lists","text":"Dynamic hotkey lists","level":3},{"id":"metadata-name-description-and-group","text":"Metadata (name, description, and group)","level":2},{"id":"introspecting-registrations","text":"Introspecting registrations","level":2},{"id":"the-hotkey-manager","text":"The hotkey manager","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe `injectHotkey` API is the primary way to register keyboard shortcuts in Angular applications. It wraps the singleton `HotkeyManager` with injection-context lifecycle management and Angular signal-friendly reactive options.\n\n## Logical keys and physical positions\n\nUse a logical binding when the shortcut should follow the character on the active layout. Use a physical binding when it should follow a keyboard position:\n\n| Binding | Identity checked |\n| --- | --- |\n| `Mod+S` or `{ key: 'S', mod: true }` | Logical `event.key`, with conservative code fallback |\n| `Mod+[KeyS]` or `{ code: 'KeyS', mod: true }` | Exact `event.code` |\n| `Enter` | Logical Enter, including numpad Enter |\n| `[Enter]` / `[NumpadEnter]` | Separate physical Enter positions |\n\nEvery physical code uses brackets in strings, including names shared with logical keys such as `[Enter]` and `[F13]`. Supported codes are type-safe and available in autocomplete. Do not put a bracketed code in an object's `key` field; use `code`. A binding has either `key` or `code`, never both.\n\nOn a layout where the `KeyQ` position produces `a`, `A` follows that character and `[KeyQ]` follows the position. Logical ASCII letters remain layout-aware; conservative physical fallback helps with transformed output such as macOS Option keys. Exact matches take priority over weaker fallbacks among eligible registrations on the same target.\n\nCallbacks expose the same distinction in `context.parsedHotkey`: check `parsed.code !== undefined` before reading its physical identity. Use `formatForDisplay` for labels; stored physical strings retain their brackets.\n\n## Basic usage\n\n```ts\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectHotkey } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\n@Component({ standalone: true, template: `` })\nexport class AppComponent {\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkey('Mod+S', () => {\n      saveDocument()\n    })\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe callback receives the original `KeyboardEvent` as the first argument and a `HotkeyCallbackContext` as the second:\n\n```ts\ninjectHotkey('Mod+S', (event, context) => {\n  console.log(context.hotkey)\n  console.log(context.parsedHotkey)\n})\n```\n\n### Changing a binding\n\nPass a new logical or physical binding through your framework's normal state mechanism. A recorder result such as `Alt+[KeyS]` can be passed directly to the same registration API. Keep an initial binding in application state if you want a reset button; the library does not need a separate preferences store.\n\n## Property getters\n\nProperty getters and functions returning an options object are both supported. Read reactive state inside the getter. A plain value such as `{ enabled: currentValue }` captures the value when that object is created.\n\nThe adapter reads option properties inside its reactive computation and updates registrations automatically. Callbacks such as `onRecord` and `onCancel` remain functions; the adapter does not call them to resolve options. Tracking is shallow; callback bodies and nested objects are not evaluated to discover dependencies. Keep getters free of side effects. Ordinary option changes preserve registration identity. Changing the target moves the registration to that target.\n\n```ts\nimport { Component, signal } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectHotkey } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\n@Component({ selector: 'save-shortcut', template: '' })\nexport class SaveShortcut {\n\tenabled = signal(true)\n\n\tconstructor() {\n\t\tconst component = this\n\t\tinjectHotkey('Mod+S', () => console.log('Save'), {\n\t\t\tget enabled() {\n\t\t\t\treturn component.enabled()\n\t\t\t},\n\t\t})\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nYou can also pass `() => ({ enabled: this.enabled() })` from the component. Signals read by option getters update registrations when Angular runs the effect. Use the same forms for common options, per-definition options, sequences, and recorders. Getter properties in provided defaults are tracked too.\n\n## Default options\n\n`injectHotkey` uses the same core defaults as the framework-agnostic manager:\n\n```ts\ninjectHotkey('Mod+S', callback, {\n  enabled: true,\n  preventDefault: true,\n  stopPropagation: true,\n  eventType: 'keydown',\n  requireReset: false,\n  ignoreInputs: undefined,\n  target: document,\n  platform: undefined,\n  conflictBehavior: 'warn',\n})\n```\n\n## Reactive options\n\nFor reactive state, pass an options object with property getters or a function returning options.\n\n### `enabled`\n\nWhen `enabled` is false, the hotkey stays registered (visible in devtools); only the callback is suppressed.\n\n```ts\nimport { Component, signal } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectHotkey } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\n@Component({ standalone: true, template: `` })\nexport class EditorComponent {\n  readonly isEditing = signal(false)\n\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkey('Mod+S', () => save(), () => ({\n      enabled: this.isEditing(),\n    }))\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### `target`\n\n```ts\nimport { Component, ElementRef, viewChild } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectHotkey } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\n@Component({\n  standalone: true,\n  template: `<div #panel tabindex=\"0\">Panel content</div>`,\n})\nexport class PanelComponent {\n  private readonly panel = viewChild<ElementRef<HTMLDivElement>>('panel')\n\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkey('Escape', () => closePanel(), () => ({\n      target: this.panel()?.nativeElement ?? null,\n    }))\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Global defaults via provider\n\n```ts\nimport { ApplicationConfig } from '@angular/core'\nimport { provideHotkeys } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\nexport const appConfig: ApplicationConfig = {\n  providers: [\n    provideHotkeys({\n      hotkey: { preventDefault: false, ignoreInputs: false },\n    }),\n  ],\n}\n```\n\n## Common options\n\n### `requireReset`\n\n```ts\ninjectHotkey('Escape', () => closePanel(), { requireReset: true })\n```\n\n### `ignoreInputs`\n\n```ts\ninjectHotkey('K', () => openSearch())\ninjectHotkey('Enter', () => submit(), { ignoreInputs: false })\n```\n\n### `conflictBehavior`\n\n```ts\ninjectHotkey('Mod+S', () => save(), { conflictBehavior: 'replace' })\n```\n\n### `platform`\n\n```ts\ninjectHotkey('Mod+S', () => save(), { platform: 'mac' })\n```\n\n## Automatic cleanup\n\nRegistrations are cleaned up automatically when the owning injection context is destroyed.\n\n## Registering multiple hotkeys\n\nWhen you need to register several hotkeys at once, or a dynamic list of variable length, use `injectHotkeys` (plural):\n\n```ts\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectHotkeys } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\n@Component({ standalone: true, template: `` })\nexport class EditorComponent {\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkeys([\n      { hotkey: 'Mod+S', callback: () => this.save() },\n      { hotkey: 'Mod+Z', callback: () => this.undo() },\n      { hotkey: 'Escape', callback: () => this.close() },\n    ])\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Common options with per-hotkey overrides\n\nPass shared options as the second argument. Per-definition options override the common ones:\n\n```ts\ninjectHotkeys(\n  [\n    { hotkey: 'Mod+S', callback: () => this.save() },\n    { hotkey: 'Mod+Z', callback: () => this.undo(), options: { enabled: false } },\n  ],\n  { preventDefault: true },\n)\n```\n\n### Dynamic hotkey lists\n\nPass a getter for reactive arrays driven by Angular signals:\n\n```ts\nshortcuts = signal([...])\n\nconstructor() {\n  injectHotkeys(\n    () => this.shortcuts().map((s) => ({\n      hotkey: s.key,\n      callback: s.action,\n    })),\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe function tracks signal dependencies and diffs registrations automatically.\n\n## Metadata (name, description, and group)\n\nEvery hotkey registration can carry a `meta` object with a `name`, `description`, and `group`. Metadata never affects hotkey behavior, but it flows through to registrations and devtools, so you can build shortcut palettes and help screens from it.\n\n```ts\ninjectHotkey('Mod+S', () => save(), {\n  meta: { name: 'Save', description: 'Save the document' },\n})\n```\n\nThe `meta` option is typed as `HotkeyMeta`, which ships with `name`, `description`, and `group` fields. You can extend it with additional properties using TypeScript declaration merging:\n\n```ts\ndeclare module '@tanstack/hotkeys' {\n  interface HotkeyMeta {\n    icon?: string\n  }\n}\n\ninjectHotkey('Mod+S', () => save(), {\n  meta: { name: 'Save', description: 'Save the document', icon: 'floppy', group: 'File' },\n})\n```\n\nGroup is descriptive metadata, not an execution scope. A shortcuts panel can group live registration views directly. Disabled registrations remain listed; unmounted registrations disappear.\n\n## Introspecting registrations\n\nUse the `injectHotkeyRegistrations` API to get a live view of all hotkey and sequence registrations. Use it to build shortcut palettes, help dialogs, or devtools.\n\n```ts\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectHotkeyRegistrations, formatForDisplay } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\n@Component({\n  standalone: true,\n  template: `\n    <h2>Keyboard Shortcuts</h2>\n    <ul>\n      @for (reg of registrations().hotkeys; track reg.id) {\n        <li>\n          <kbd>{{ formatForDisplay(reg.hotkey) }}</kbd>\n          @if (reg.options.meta?.name) {\n            <span> — {{ reg.options.meta.name }}</span>\n          }\n          @if (reg.options.meta?.description) {\n            <p>{{ reg.options.meta.description }}</p>\n          }\n        </li>\n      }\n    </ul>\n    @if (registrations().sequences.length > 0) {\n      <h2>Sequences</h2>\n      <ul>\n        @for (reg of registrations().sequences; track reg.id) {\n          <li>\n            <kbd>{{ displaySequence(reg.sequence) }}</kbd>\n            @if (reg.options.meta?.name) {\n              <span> — {{ reg.options.meta.name }}</span>\n            }\n          </li>\n        }\n      </ul>\n    }\n  `,\n})\nexport class ShortcutPaletteComponent {\n  readonly formatForDisplay = formatForDisplay\n  readonly displaySequence = (sequence: ReadonlyArray<Parameters<typeof formatForDisplay>[0]>) =>\n    sequence.map((step) => formatForDisplay(step)).join(' → ')\n  readonly registrations = injectHotkeyRegistrations()\n}\n```\n\nThe returned signal holds an object with two arrays. `hotkeys` contains registration objects with the hotkey string, options (including `meta`), and enabled state. `sequences` contains sequence registrations with the same structure.\n\n## The hotkey manager\n\nYou can access the underlying manager directly when needed:\n\n```ts\nimport { getHotkeyManager } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\nconst manager = getHotkeyManager()\nmanager.isRegistered('Mod+S')\nmanager.getRegistrationCount()\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Hotkeys Guide\nid: hotkeys\n---\n\nThe `injectHotkey` API is the primary way to register keyboard shortcuts in Angular applications. It wraps the singleton `HotkeyManager` with injection-context lifecycle management and Angular signal-friendly reactive options.\n\n## Logical keys and physical positions\n\nUse a logical binding when the shortcut should follow the character on the active layout. Use a physical binding when it should follow a keyboard position:\n\n| Binding | Identity checked |\n| --- | --- |\n| `Mod+S` or `{ key: 'S', mod: true }` | Logical `event.key`, with conservative code fallback |\n| `Mod+[KeyS]` or `{ code: 'KeyS', mod: true }` | Exact `event.code` |\n| `Enter` | Logical Enter, including numpad Enter |\n| `[Enter]` / `[NumpadEnter]` | Separate physical Enter positions |\n\nEvery physical code uses brackets in strings, including names shared with logical keys such as `[Enter]` and `[F13]`. Supported codes are type-safe and available in autocomplete. Do not put a bracketed code in an object's `key` field; use `code`. A binding has either `key` or `code`, never both.\n\nOn a layout where the `KeyQ` position produces `a`, `A` follows that character and `[KeyQ]` follows the position. Logical ASCII letters remain layout-aware; conservative physical fallback helps with transformed output such as macOS Option keys. Exact matches take priority over weaker fallbacks among eligible registrations on the same target.\n\nCallbacks expose the same distinction in `context.parsedHotkey`: check `parsed.code !== undefined` before reading its physical identity. Use `formatForDisplay` for labels; stored physical strings retain their brackets.\n\n## Basic usage\n\n```ts\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectHotkey } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\n@Component({ standalone: true, template: `` })\nexport class AppComponent {\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkey('Mod+S', () => {\n      saveDocument()\n    })\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe callback receives the original `KeyboardEvent` as the first argument and a `HotkeyCallbackContext` as the second:\n\n```ts\ninjectHotkey('Mod+S', (event, context) => {\n  console.log(context.hotkey)\n  console.log(context.parsedHotkey)\n})\n```\n\n### Changing a binding\n\nPass a new logical or physical binding through your framework's normal state mechanism. A recorder result such as `Alt+[KeyS]` can be passed directly to the same registration API. Keep an initial binding in application state if you want a reset button; the library does not need a separate preferences store.\n\n## Property getters\n\nProperty getters and functions returning an options object are both supported. Read reactive state inside the getter. A plain value such as `{ enabled: currentValue }` captures the value when that object is created.\n\nThe adapter reads option properties inside its reactive computation and updates registrations automatically. Callbacks such as `onRecord` and `onCancel` remain functions; the adapter does not call them to resolve options. Tracking is shallow; callback bodies and nested objects are not evaluated to discover dependencies. Keep getters free of side effects. Ordinary option changes preserve registration identity. Changing the target moves the registration to that target.\n\n```ts\nimport { Component, signal } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectHotkey } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\n@Component({ selector: 'save-shortcut', template: '' })\nexport class SaveShortcut {\n\tenabled = signal(true)\n\n\tconstructor() {\n\t\tconst component = this\n\t\tinjectHotkey('Mod+S', () => console.log('Save'), {\n\t\t\tget enabled() {\n\t\t\t\treturn component.enabled()\n\t\t\t},\n\t\t})\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nYou can also pass `() => ({ enabled: this.enabled() })` from the component. Signals read by option getters update registrations when Angular runs the effect. Use the same forms for common options, per-definition options, sequences, and recorders. Getter properties in provided defaults are tracked too.\n\n## Default options\n\n`injectHotkey` uses the same core defaults as the framework-agnostic manager:\n\n```ts\ninjectHotkey('Mod+S', callback, {\n  enabled: true,\n  preventDefault: true,\n  stopPropagation: true,\n  eventType: 'keydown',\n  requireReset: false,\n  ignoreInputs: undefined,\n  target: document,\n  platform: undefined,\n  conflictBehavior: 'warn',\n})\n```\n\n## Reactive options\n\nFor reactive state, pass an options object with property getters or a function returning options.\n\n### `enabled`\n\nWhen `enabled` is false, the hotkey stays registered (visible in devtools); only the callback is suppressed.\n\n```ts\nimport { Component, signal } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectHotkey } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\n@Component({ standalone: true, template: `` })\nexport class EditorComponent {\n  readonly isEditing = signal(false)\n\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkey('Mod+S', () => save(), () => ({\n      enabled: this.isEditing(),\n    }))\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### `target`\n\n```ts\nimport { Component, ElementRef, viewChild } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectHotkey } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\n@Component({\n  standalone: true,\n  template: `<div #panel tabindex=\"0\">Panel content</div>`,\n})\nexport class PanelComponent {\n  private readonly panel = viewChild<ElementRef<HTMLDivElement>>('panel')\n\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkey('Escape', () => closePanel(), () => ({\n      target: this.panel()?.nativeElement ?? null,\n    }))\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Global defaults via provider\n\n```ts\nimport { ApplicationConfig } from '@angular/core'\nimport { provideHotkeys } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\nexport const appConfig: ApplicationConfig = {\n  providers: [\n    provideHotkeys({\n      hotkey: { preventDefault: false, ignoreInputs: false },\n    }),\n  ],\n}\n```\n\n## Common options\n\n### `requireReset`\n\n```ts\ninjectHotkey('Escape', () => closePanel(), { requireReset: true })\n```\n\n### `ignoreInputs`\n\n```ts\ninjectHotkey('K', () => openSearch())\ninjectHotkey('Enter', () => submit(), { ignoreInputs: false })\n```\n\n### `conflictBehavior`\n\n```ts\ninjectHotkey('Mod+S', () => save(), { conflictBehavior: 'replace' })\n```\n\n### `platform`\n\n```ts\ninjectHotkey('Mod+S', () => save(), { platform: 'mac' })\n```\n\n## Automatic cleanup\n\nRegistrations are cleaned up automatically when the owning injection context is destroyed.\n\n## Registering multiple hotkeys\n\nWhen you need to register several hotkeys at once, or a dynamic list of variable length, use `injectHotkeys` (plural):\n\n```ts\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectHotkeys } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\n@Component({ standalone: true, template: `` })\nexport class EditorComponent {\n  constructor() {\n    injectHotkeys([\n      { hotkey: 'Mod+S', callback: () => this.save() },\n      { hotkey: 'Mod+Z', callback: () => this.undo() },\n      { hotkey: 'Escape', callback: () => this.close() },\n    ])\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Common options with per-hotkey overrides\n\nPass shared options as the second argument. Per-definition options override the common ones:\n\n```ts\ninjectHotkeys(\n  [\n    { hotkey: 'Mod+S', callback: () => this.save() },\n    { hotkey: 'Mod+Z', callback: () => this.undo(), options: { enabled: false } },\n  ],\n  { preventDefault: true },\n)\n```\n\n### Dynamic hotkey lists\n\nPass a getter for reactive arrays driven by Angular signals:\n\n```ts\nshortcuts = signal([...])\n\nconstructor() {\n  injectHotkeys(\n    () => this.shortcuts().map((s) => ({\n      hotkey: s.key,\n      callback: s.action,\n    })),\n  )\n}\n```\n\nThe function tracks signal dependencies and diffs registrations automatically.\n\n## Metadata (name, description, and group)\n\nEvery hotkey registration can carry a `meta` object with a `name`, `description`, and `group`. Metadata never affects hotkey behavior, but it flows through to registrations and devtools, so you can build shortcut palettes and help screens from it.\n\n```ts\ninjectHotkey('Mod+S', () => save(), {\n  meta: { name: 'Save', description: 'Save the document' },\n})\n```\n\nThe `meta` option is typed as `HotkeyMeta`, which ships with `name`, `description`, and `group` fields. You can extend it with additional properties using TypeScript declaration merging:\n\n```ts\ndeclare module '@tanstack/hotkeys' {\n  interface HotkeyMeta {\n    icon?: string\n  }\n}\n\ninjectHotkey('Mod+S', () => save(), {\n  meta: { name: 'Save', description: 'Save the document', icon: 'floppy', group: 'File' },\n})\n```\n\nGroup is descriptive metadata, not an execution scope. A shortcuts panel can group live registration views directly. Disabled registrations remain listed; unmounted registrations disappear.\n\n## Introspecting registrations\n\nUse the `injectHotkeyRegistrations` API to get a live view of all hotkey and sequence registrations. Use it to build shortcut palettes, help dialogs, or devtools.\n\n```ts\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport { injectHotkeyRegistrations, formatForDisplay } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\n@Component({\n  standalone: true,\n  template: `\n    <h2>Keyboard Shortcuts</h2>\n    <ul>\n      @for (reg of registrations().hotkeys; track reg.id) {\n        <li>\n          <kbd>{{ formatForDisplay(reg.hotkey) }}</kbd>\n          @if (reg.options.meta?.name) {\n            <span> — {{ reg.options.meta.name }}</span>\n          }\n          @if (reg.options.meta?.description) {\n            <p>{{ reg.options.meta.description }}</p>\n          }\n        </li>\n      }\n    </ul>\n    @if (registrations().sequences.length > 0) {\n      <h2>Sequences</h2>\n      <ul>\n        @for (reg of registrations().sequences; track reg.id) {\n          <li>\n            <kbd>{{ displaySequence(reg.sequence) }}</kbd>\n            @if (reg.options.meta?.name) {\n              <span> — {{ reg.options.meta.name }}</span>\n            }\n          </li>\n        }\n      </ul>\n    }\n  `,\n})\nexport class ShortcutPaletteComponent {\n  readonly formatForDisplay = formatForDisplay\n  readonly displaySequence = (sequence: ReadonlyArray<Parameters<typeof formatForDisplay>[0]>) =>\n    sequence.map((step) => formatForDisplay(step)).join(' → ')\n  readonly registrations = injectHotkeyRegistrations()\n}\n```\n\nThe returned signal holds an object with two arrays. `hotkeys` contains registration objects with the hotkey string, options (including `meta`), and enabled state. `sequences` contains sequence registrations with the same structure.\n\n## The hotkey manager\n\nYou can access the underlying manager directly when needed:\n\n```ts\nimport { getHotkeyManager } from '@tanstack/angular-hotkeys'\n\nconst manager = getHotkeyManager()\nmanager.isRegistered('Mod+S')\nmanager.getRegistrationCount()\n```\n"}
